<%# Stripeclub's own pagination, and it should not have to be.

    its_swiss/shared/_pagination renders exactly this markup and cannot be
    used. Its documentation comment contains a worked example written in ERB,
    and the closing delimiter of that example ends the comment early — so the
    remaining prose is emitted as page content. "Long runs are elided around
    the current page, because a hundred numbers is not a control." appeared
    above the page numbers, with a stray delimiter after it.

    Writing this note cost the same mistake twice: a comment describing the
    bug cannot quote the syntax that causes it. Hence no example here.

    This is the library's markup, copied, with nothing changed but the comment
    that broke it. Delete this file and render the library's partial again as
    soon as the gem is fixed. See ITS-SWISS-CANDIDATES.md.
%>
<% numbers = its_swiss_page_numbers(page, pages, window: local_assigns.fetch(:window, 2)) %>
<% if pages > 1 %>
  <nav class="pagination" aria-label="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:label, "Pages") %>">
    <% numbers.each do |number| %>
      <% if number.nil? %>
        <span class="pagination__gap" aria-hidden="true">…</span>
      <% elsif number == page %>
        <span aria-current="page"><%= number %></span>
      <% else %>
        <%= link_to number, url.call(number) %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </nav>
<% end %>
